  "id": "osf-symlink-resolution",
  "generatedAt": "2026-10-07T12:20:31.227Z",
  "title": "Symlink resolution for osf check and scan",
  "summary": "Adds a shared `symlink` module that decides what a symlink means to the scanner: a link whose real target lives inside the repository is followed to the real files behind it, while a link pointing outside the repository, into `.git`, at nothing, or in a loop is refused with a named error. `check scan`, `lint-writing` and `lint-skill` now expand their explicit paths through this module before the existing not-found check, and the directory walker in `scan` follows in-repo links instead of counting them as skipped. The net effect is that the `.claude/skills -> ../.agents/skills` layout is scanned for real, and a scan of nothing but symlinks is no longer silently clean.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
